From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:37:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] docs(workflow): Trace dialog shows the band in use,
 Join gaps and Alt+T (ADR-396)

F-A15 lists Alt+T for Trace Image and Option+M for Measure on macOS.
F-E1 says how to open Trace Image, what Detection shows in automatic
modes and where Manual starts, which grid pixel settings count on, which
kept adjustments a style uses, that Edge Detection previews and exports
as strokes like Centerline, and names the Join gaps control.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sve7yAMGfoSkUWytefCLp2
---
 WORKFLOW.md | 38 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/WORKFLOW.md b/WORKFLOW.md
index 5b72eee0d..9f27ae168 100644
--- a/WORKFLOW.md
+++ b/WORKFLOW.md
@@ -905,7 +905,9 @@ Mac uses `Cmd`, Windows/Linux web uses `Ctrl`.
 - `Cmd/Ctrl+R` - Rectangle
 - `Cmd/Ctrl+E` - Ellipse
 - `Cmd/Ctrl+L` - Line/pen
-- `Alt+M` - Measure
+- `Alt+M` - Measure (Option+M on macOS)
+- `Alt+T` - Trace Image (Option+T on macOS; LightBurn's binding; no-op unless the selected
+  object is a raster image)
 - `Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+B` - Convert to Bitmap (LightBurn's binding; no-op unless a
   single convertible vector is selected)
 
@@ -2290,7 +2292,8 @@ settings and Job Review keep their existing read-only setup references.
